# This tree is shared between a Mac and a Windows box through git. Windows git ships
# with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites every line of every file on checkout and
# back again on commit. That is survivable for a 200-line Luau file and catastrophic
# for an 8 MB generated .rbxmx: a clone that changed nothing shows up as a whole-file
# diff, and the two machines start disagreeing about files neither of them edited.
# Normalise to LF everywhere so the bytes on disk are the same on both platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated Roblox model XML. These are machine-written by tools/gen_*.py, they are
# large, and a line-level merge of one is not something a human can resolve -- the
# correct fix for a conflict here is always to regenerate, never to hand-edit. Mark
# them binary so git refuses the merge outright instead of producing a plausible-
# looking file with half of each map in it.
*.rbxmx -text -diff merge=binary
*.rbxl  -text -diff
*.rbxlx -text -diff

# Shell scripts must keep LF even if someone forces CRLF globally -- a CRLF shebang
# line fails with a "bad interpreter" error that names a binary that plainly exists.
*.sh text eol=lf
